  "_skill_md": "---\nname: vercel\ndescription: Internal API for vercel\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://vercel.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Bearer Token\"\n  endpointCount: 16\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Vercel API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nBearer Token — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (2)\n- `GET /api/v2/teams/{teamToken}` — Authenticate and retrieve team information.\n- `GET /auth-redirect/unknown-slug` — Initiate an authentication redirect flow.\n\n### Data Read (7)\n- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve data for a specific resource ID.\n- `GET /api/v1/frameworks` — Retrieve a list of supported frameworks.\n- `GET /api/v1/microfrontends/groups` — Get a list of microfrontend groups.\n- `GET /api/v1/notifications/push` — Get push notification settings.\n- `GET /api/v2/dashboard/projects` — Get a list of projects for the dashboard.\n- `GET /api/www/user` — Get the current user's profile information.\n- `GET /new/templates` — Fetch available project templates.\n\n### Data Write (1)\n- `POST /{hash}/{id}` — Write data to a specific resource.\n\n### Search (1)\n- `GET /api/v1/integrations/search-repo` — Search for repositories.\n\n### Media (1)\n- `GET /api/v1/integrations/github/file-tree/billy872/mission-control` — Get a file tree from a GitHub repository.\n\n### Realtime (3)\n- `POST /api/stream/internal/statsig` — Send internal statistics via stream.\n- `POST /hfi/events/{eventId}` — Post events to a realtime stream.\n- `POST /rs/stream/v1/page` — Stream page view data.\n\n### Core API (1)\n- `GET /api/{apiId}` — Access a generic Vercel API endpoint.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"vercel\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few examples to get you started with the Vercel API:\n\n```typescript\n// Get the current user's profile information.\nasync function getUserProfile() {\n  const user = await client.getApiWwwUser();\n  console.log(user);\n  return user;\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Retrieve a list of projects for the dashboard.\nasync function getDashboardProjects() {\n  const projects = await client.getApiV2DashboardProjects();\n  console.log(projects);\n  return projects;\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Write data to a specific resource (example - replace with actual hash and ID).\nasync function writeData(hash: string, id: string, data: any) {\n  const response = await client.postHashId({ hash, id, data });\n  console.log(response);\n  return response;\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Bearer Token\n**Base URL:** `https://vercel.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 4 auth headers\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Vercel's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Vercel data without official API access\n- Automate actions on vercel.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Vercel frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { VercelClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await VercelClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 4 (authorization, x-csrf-token, livepipeline-session, x-twitter-auth-type)\n- **Session cookies:** 0\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (38)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
